# Spec for tools/riscpkg.py: Groove.
Package: Groove
Section: Audio
Priority: Optional
Licence: Free
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Standards-Version: 0.4.0
Environment: arm32, vfpv3
Depends: SharedUnixLibrary (>= 1.16), ARMEABISupport
Recommends: SoftMIDI
Components: Apps.Audio.!Groove (Movable LookAt)
Homepage: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-groove
Description: Music studio: loops, drums, piano roll, recording
 Drag loops into a song, play instruments from the computer keyboard,
 draw beats in a step grid and notes in a piano roll, with a lane for
 controllers and pitch bend; record what you play, mix up to 32 tracks
 and export a WAV. MIDI import and export, MIDI out with a channel and
 program for each track, and Maestro files play as Maestro plays them.
 With SoftMIDI, any track can use a SoundFont's General MIDI
 instruments and drum kits. A User guide with pictures is on the icon
 bar menu.
Build-Map: !Groove -> Apps/Audio/!Groove
Build-Notice: Groove, packaged for PackMan from the release zip on
 https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-groove/releases
 .
 Groove is under the MIT licence. It links SoftMIDI's libmidisynth and
 TinySoundFont (MIT), stb_vorbis (MIT or public domain) and UnixLib
 (parts under the LGPL; the repository at tag v0.3 is the source to
 rebuild Groove with). The notices follow.
